    {
      "id": "question-expand-01",
      "intent": "expand",
      "parentIntent": "question",
      "lessonKey": "ai-prompting-iteration",
      "parentSampleId": "question-01",
      "blockId": "aiess-l09-b054",
      "output": "A vague goal is the most common trap. You might say \"summarize this supplier report\" but forget whether you need a one-liner for a meeting or a full memo with risks flagged. The model then guesses, wastes effort on detail you do not need, or misses what matters. Constraints are easier to fix once you see bad output, but a fuzzy goal usually means starting over. The sharper move is to spend thirty seconds writing down what success looks like before you prompt, then build your instructions backward from that picture. When you tried a prompt recently and the output missed the mark, was it because you were unsure what you wanted, or because you did not tell the model how to format the answer?",
      "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5",
