      "parentSampleId": "question-02",
      "blockId": "aiess-l07-b042",
      "output": "Think of it like hearing someone speak fluently about a topic they've never studied, they sound certain while guessing. The model does the same thing. It learned patterns from text, so it arranges words smoothly and logically, but smooth arrangement doesn't mean facts are correct. A hallucination happens when the model invents or distorts information confidently because the pattern looks right, even though no source backs it up. You still need to verify what matters. Which part feels contradictory to you?",
