      "blockId": "aiess-l01-b006",
      "output": "Getting the AI to understand routine work is harder than it sounds because the work itself changes depending on context. A supplier update looks different in a crisis than in normal times, and the AI needs to learn those shifts or it will give advice that fits the textbook but fails in practice. Training people to check the output reliably is the second trap because checking takes discipline, and discipline fades when nothing goes wrong for weeks. The third piece, deciding who owns the final call, is hardest to live by because under pressure people either blame the AI for a bad outcome or skip the check entirely. Which of these three have you seen cause real problems in your work?",
