    {
      "id": "capstone-expand-02",
      "intent": "expand",
      "parentIntent": "capstone",
      "lessonKey": "capstone",
      "parentSampleId": "capstone-03",
      "output": "Invented dates are a real problem because the model can sound confident while being completely wrong. If nine of ten reports fail that way, your prompt isn't constraining the model strongly enough. You need to add a rule like \"only use dates explicitly mentioned in the source document\" and then test again with a fresh set of reports. One failure might be noise, but nine tells you the approach itself is broken and needs a different guardrail. The key is catching these patterns through systematic testing rather than assuming early success means the method works. What does your current prompt say about where dates should come from?",
      "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5",
      "promptHash": "e22fa556fbc0f80bfbc9fb472d94a5218900c046a18e5cc81f849ed0c0028313",
